Tom: Ah, in France that sign can mean zero, or "worthless". It''s easy to get wrong.
Mia: Really? At home it just means everything is fine.
Tom: Yes, but the same gesture differs from country to country.
Mia: So what should I do when I travel?
Tom: Watch the local people and avoid making gestures you''re not sure about.
Mia: That''s good advice. I''ll be more careful next time.
Tom: Don''t worry. Everyone makes mistakes like this when learning about a new culture.', 'Mia 在法国对服务员比"OK"手势,对方不高兴;Tom 解释在法国那手势可能表示零或"没价值";同一手势因国家而异;Tom 建议旅行时观察当地人、不确定的手势就别比;Mia 表示以后会更小心。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did the \"OK\" sign seem to mean in France?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Zero, or \"worthless\".","That everything is fine.","A number ten.","A polite hello."]},{"q":"Why did the waiter look upset?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Mia spoke too loudly.","He understood the rude meaning of the sign.","He could not find the table.","Mia did not pay the bill."]},{"q":"What does Tom say about the same gesture?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It differs from country to country.","It means the same everywhere.","It has no meaning at all.","It is always rude."]},{"q":"What advice does Tom give for travelling?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Never use any gestures.","Watch local people and avoid unsure gestures.","Make every gesture loudly.","Speak only English."]},{"q":"How does Tom make Mia feel better?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He tells her to go home.","He laughs at her.","He says everyone makes such mistakes when learning a culture.","He says France is a bad place."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U4');
It can help us get through difficult moments and find friends among strangers.
We use a smile to greet people, to apologise, or to ask for help.
A warm smile can even break down barriers that words cannot.
So if you feel down, try smiling, and you may slowly feel better.', '微笑也许是我们最有力的肢体语言;它能帮我们度过难关、在陌生人中找到朋友;我们用微笑问候、道歉或求助;温暖的微笑甚至能打破言语打不破的隔阂;心情低落时不妨微笑,你会慢慢好起来。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the speaker call a smile?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A useless habit.","A foreign word.","A kind of food.","The most powerful piece of body language."]},{"q":"What can a smile help us do in hard moments?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Get through difficult moments and find friends.","Forget our names.","Win every game.","Speak a new language."]},{"q":"Which use of a smile is mentioned?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To start a fight.","To greet, apologise or ask for help.","To hide money.","To end all friendships."]},{"q":"What can a warm smile break down?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A strong wall of stone.","All spoken words.","Barriers that words cannot.","The price of things."]},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest doing when you feel down?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop talking to everyone.","Stay alone all day.","Never leave your room.","Try smiling, and you may feel better."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U4');
Sara: They''re hard! We have to show feelings using only our faces and hands.
Ben: That does sound difficult. Can people guess what you mean?
Sara: Sometimes. Last week I tried to show "I''m tired", but they thought I was sad.
Ben: Well, tired and sad can look quite similar.
Sara: True. I''m still not very confident about my silent acting.
Ben: Don''t give up. It''s good you tried — it takes practice.
Sara: Thanks. I''ll keep practising and watch real people more closely.', 'Ben 问 Sara 无声表演课怎么样;Sara 说很难,只能用脸和手表达感受;上周想演"我累了",观众却以为是"难过";Ben 说累和难过看起来确实相似;Sara 对自己的无声表演还不太自信;Ben 鼓励她别放弃、要多练;Sara 决定继续练习并多观察真人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is special about Sara''s acting classes?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They act without speaking.","They only sing songs.","They write long essays.","They use lots of words."]},{"q":"What does Sara use to show feelings?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A microphone.","Only her face and hands.","A long speech.","A music player."]},{"q":"What happened when Sara tried to show \"I''m tired\"?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Everyone guessed it at once.","Nobody watched her.","People thought she was sad.","She forgot the scene."]},{"q":"How does Sara feel about her silent acting?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Very proud and sure.","Bored and angry.","Too excited to act.","Not very confident."]},{"q":"What does Ben tell Sara at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It''s good she tried; it takes practice.","She should stop the classes.","Acting is a waste of time.","She will never improve."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U4');
When students lean forward and look up, I know they are interested.
When a student keeps looking at the clock, he is probably bored.
Students who cross their arms tightly may feel worried or afraid.
Their quiet body language tells me when to slow down or offer help.', '作为老师,我只看学生的身体就能了解很多;学生前倾抬头时,我知道他们感兴趣;学生总看钟,多半是无聊了;紧紧交叉双臂的学生可能感到担忧或害怕;这些安静的肢体语言告诉我何时该放慢节奏或提供帮助。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How does the teacher learn about students?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["By reading their letters.","By watching their body language.","By asking their parents.","By looking at their bags."]},{"q":"What shows that students are interested?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They fall asleep.","They leave the room.","They lean forward and look up.","They cover their faces."]},{"q":"What does looking at the clock probably mean?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The student is very proud.","The student is excited.","The student is hungry.","The student is bored."]},{"q":"What may tightly crossed arms suggest?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Worry or fear.","Great happiness.","Strong interest.","A wish to sing."]},{"q":"What does the quiet body language help the teacher decide?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Which student is richest.","When to slow down or offer help.","What to eat for lunch.","How to end the school."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U4');
Jack: Oh, sorry! I didn''t mean to be rude. I was just checking the time.
Anna: I see. I thought it meant you were bored.
Jack: In other words, my body sent the wrong message?
Anna: Exactly. Body language can be easy to misread.
Jack: So next time I should explain, or just put my watch away.
Anna: That would help. Asking "what do you mean?" can clear things up too.
Jack: Good idea. It''s better to ask than to guess wrongly.', 'Anna 问 Jack 演讲时看表是什么意思;Jack 道歉,说只是看时间、无意失礼;Anna 以为那表示无聊;Jack 说也就是他的身体传错了信息;Anna 说肢体语言容易被误读;Jack 决定下次解释或收起手表;Anna 说直接问"你什么意思"也能澄清;Jack 同意,问比猜错好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Jack do during Anna''s talk?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He fell asleep.","He left the room.","He looked at his watch.","He sang a song."]},{"q":"Why did Jack really look at his watch?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He was very bored.","He wanted to leave.","He was angry with Anna.","He was just checking the time."]},{"q":"What did Anna first think his action meant?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He was bored.","He was excited.","He was hungry.","He was proud."]},{"q":"What does Anna say about body language?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is always clear.","It can be easy to misread.","It needs no attention.","It means nothing."]},{"q":"What do they agree is a good way to clear things up?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Saying nothing at all.","Guessing the meaning quickly.","Asking what the other person means.","Leaving without a word."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U4');
Remember that a friendly gesture at home may be rude in another country.
Before you use a gesture, watch how the local people behave.
Keep your eye contact polite, not too long and not too short.
When in doubt, a warm smile is welcome almost everywhere.', '给旅行者几条关于肢体语言的小贴士:记住在本国友好的手势在别国可能无礼;用手势前先观察当地人怎么做;眼神接触要适度,别太久也别太短;拿不准时,温暖的微笑几乎处处受欢迎。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who are these tips for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only teachers.","Only children.","Only actors.","Travellers."]},{"q":"What should you remember about a friendly gesture?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It may be rude in another country.","It is rude everywhere.","It always means money.","It has no meaning abroad."]},{"q":"What should you do before using a gesture?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Make it as big as possible.","Watch how local people behave.","Use it many times quickly.","Ask everyone to copy you."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about eye contact?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Make it as long as you can.","Avoid it completely.","Keep it polite, not too long or short.","Stare hard at everyone."]},{"q":"What is welcome almost everywhere when in doubt?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A loud shout.","A long stare.","A rude sign.","A warm smile."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U4');

